{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Local code-review preview: PASS with 0 blocking and 5 advisory findings. Addressed the two actionable coverage gaps before push: added direct tests for GerritError during current-revision lookup and durable-tag/message lookup (both refuse with `eligibility-read-error`, no reset/comment/forced event), plus a real-client non-2xx reset test proving HTTP 503 raises GerritError with status preserved. Focused review-bot/security suite is now 160 passed; lint and typecheck remain green.\n\nDisposition of the other advisories: (1) Gerrit-first reconciliation and the second under-lock vote read are intentional correctness costs from the signed plan — stale local dedup is indistinguishable from a durable reset, and the under-lock read closes the race before voting; the candidate set is bounded by the existing events-log window. (2) `/rerun` reset+verify latency/new fail-closed statuses are the approved durability-vs-availability contract; acknowledging before them would recreate the bug. (3) the real-event-shape concern is conclusively answered by the ticket’s read-only production probe: 551 LLM-Review label events, all `comment-added`, all carrying both `patchSet.revision` and `patchSet.ref`, including neutral value-0 events."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786378297306122001,"uuid":"5faf9da4-3d06-455e-8e62-9c812ebc3197"}